Tremor Taxonomy is a five-member acoustic-electronic body-music ensemble built around the principle that one fixed pitch becomes more dramatic when a human-controlled harmonic refuses to stay on it.

**Linh Phạm** — đàn bầu, harmonic nodes, pitch-rod control, Node Pressure design.

**Ansel Krüger** — analog drums, mono bass, Rigid Witness sequencing, arrangement cuts.

**Mai Trần** — prepared Pianet, fixed pitch checkpoints, dry dyads.

**Huy Lê** — floor tom, struck steel, pipe percussion, physical grid accents.

**Clara Weiss** — bass oboe, low acoustic witnesses, breath-heavy pedals, key-noise articulation.

There is no conventional frontperson. Linh generates the elastic harmonic field; Ansel refuses to move the machine with her; Mai establishes fixed coordinates; Huy gives the grid physical weight; Clara provides acoustic stability when the synth withdraws. Live versions vary because harmonic-node contact, rod pressure, string tension, room temperature, and hand position change the beating pattern of every bend.

