# Fictional EP Tracklist

## Track 1: Gauge Eleven Bends Above the Mark

**Story & Context:** At 122 BPM, Ansel establishes a one-bar mono-bass figure built from tonic and fifth while Mai places one dry Pianet octave at the start of every fourth bar. Linh begins on a clear đàn bầu harmonic that matches the tonic, then slowly raises it until strong beating appears against the bass. Huy adds only kick, clipped snare, one floor-tom hit every eight bars, and a steel strike at the widest bend. Clara enters after the synth bass cuts for two bars, holding the original tonic on bass oboe while Linh remains above it. The track resolves when Linh returns to the original node without any chord change, fill, or filter sweep.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Analog strain gauge marked 11 with a red reference line, one thin waveform bending visibly above the mark while a second straight waveform stays fixed beneath it, lacquered đàn bầu wood and steel test equipment in shallow focus. Sparse spoken fragments limited to “gauge eleven,” “above the mark,” “hold the witness,” and “return clean.”

## Track 2: Same Node, Opposite Pressure

**Story & Context:** At 126 BPM, the rhythm loop remains nearly unchanged for the entire track. Linh performs one four-note harmonic pattern twice: the first version bends upward after every pluck, the second bends downward using identical rhythm. Mai plays the same suspended-second dyad beneath both versions. Ansel keeps the mono bass absolutely fixed and removes synth glide entirely. Huy alternates steel and dead-pipe strikes at section boundaries. Clara holds one low fifth through the reversal, making the opposite pitch arcs feel like two different harmonies built on the same notes. The central break contains no drums; only Pianet, bass oboe, and two opposing đàn bầu bends remain.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Calibration sheet with two mirrored pressure curves departing from the same center line, one rising and one falling, with a single-string instrument silhouette crossing the page. Spoken fragments limited to “same node,” “reverse pressure,” “do not move the grid,” and “mirror the bend.”

## Track 3: The Shaker Table Keeps One Frequency

**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 116 BPM and uses the sparsest EBM architecture on the EP. Ansel freezes the bass on one repeated low note while kick lands on every quarter and snare appears only on beat three. Linh plays progressively wider harmonic arcs against that single electronic frequency. Mai reduces her Pianet part from dyads to isolated witness notes. Huy uses one steel impact every sixteen bars. Clara enters only after the widest bend, sustaining a low acoustic unison with the synth. In the final minute, the machine pattern continues unchanged while Linh reduces the bend width cycle by cycle until the beating disappears. The last sound is the fixed electronic note alone for one bar, then a dry stop.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Large industrial shaker table beneath one illuminated frequency meter, a fixed horizontal line surrounded by several narrowing curved pitch traces, fluorescent laboratory haze, no motion blur. Sparse spoken fragments limited to “one frequency,” “table stays,” “narrow the tremor,” and “stop on zero.”

